SWEET WLAN level 7 firmware console (patch 0155, reads apart from the BAR2 window). Once W16 has seen the shared-area address, the firmware runs 1 s longer, then the hnd_cons_t at shared word 5 (console_addr) is read as brcmfmac does (pcie.c:828-891: buffer address +8, size +12, write index +16) and the bytes 0..write index are printed as "SWEET WLAN: FW <line>" (CR dropped, lines cut at 120 characters, other non-printable bytes as '.'), then W17 as before.
The firmware places header and buffer differently per boot (header 0x0038aba8 / 0x004367a4, buffer 0x0041533c 8192 bytes; runs wd7-oriole2/3), so both may lie anywhere in RAM: each word is read under the BAR2 window that holds it, cfg 0x84 moving between 0 and the tail window as needed (two new reusable tuples SWT_WIN2_TAIL_CON / SWT_WIN2_ZERO_CON, only after the W16 window is back at 0, old value 0 / tail, arming the window and CA restore groups) and ending at 0. A size of 0 or above 64 KiB, a buffer beyond ram_end or a write index beyond the size is logged and not read. No glue change.
Tests: shim/wlan_wr_host_test.c rune() console cases, tools/test_wlan_wr_mutants.py.

